---
import Prose from '../../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { getDocsPage } from '../../data/docs-topics';

const page = getDocsPage('cli');
---
<Prose title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path}>
  <p>The <code>writ</code> command opens files in the running app. The Windows installer and the <code>.deb</code> put it on your PATH, and <code>install.sh</code> puts it in <code>~/.local/bin</code>. On macOS or from a downloaded AppImage, install it from Settings, Integrations, Terminal command (macOS asks for an administrator password once when <code>/usr/local/bin</code> is not writable).</p>
  <pre><code>writ todo.txt            # open a file
writ .                   # open the folder
pbpaste | writ           # stdin becomes a new file
make test 2>&1 | writ --title tests</code></pre>
  <p>Piped text is saved as a file in Writ's folder, so it stays after the terminal closes.</p>

  <h2 id="links">writ:// links</h2>
  <p>On macOS and Windows, <code>writ://open?path=Plan.md&amp;line=12</code> opens a file in Writ's folder at a line, from a browser or another program, and <code>writ://new</code> opens a new tab. A link opens only a file inside the folder, and following one writes nothing.</p>
</Prose>
